1
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:03,000
You can't bury the past.

2
00:09:54,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Old Henry is a western, action, drama film directed by Potsy Ponciroli.

3
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:57,000
A widowed farmer and his son warily take in a
mysterious, injured man with a satchel of cash.

4
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:54,000
When a posse of men claiming to be the law come for the
money, the farmer must decide who to trust.

5
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Defending a siege of his homestead, the farmer reveals a talent for gun-slinging
that surprises everyone calling his true identity into question.

6
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:48,000
Henry, played by Tim Blake Nelson.

7
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:45,000
Curry, played by Scott Haze.

8
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Wyatt, played by Gavin Lewis.

9
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:39,000
Ketchum, played by Stephen Dorff.

10
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Al, played by Trace Adkins.

11
00:54:27,000 --> 00:54:33,000
Dugan, played by Richard Speight Jr..

12
00:59:24,000 --> 00:59:30,000
Old Henry is a 2021 American western action drama film
written and directed by Potsy Ponciroli.

13
01:04:21,000 --> 01:04:27,000
It stars Tim Blake Nelson as the titular character, a farmer who must protect his son from outlaws,
with Scott Haze, Gavin Lewis, Trace Adkins, and Stephen Dorff in supporting roles.

14
01:09:18,000 --> 01:09:24,000
The film had its world premiere at the Venice Film Festival on September 7,
2021, and was theatrically released in the United States by Shout!

15
01:14:15,000 --> 01:14:21,000
Studios on October 1.

16
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
It was critically acclaimed for the story, Ponciroli's
direction, and Nelson's performance.

17
01:24:09,000 --> 01:24:15,000
The National Board of Review selected the film in its annual
list of the Top Ten Independent Films of the year.

18
01:29:06,000 --> 01:29:12,000
The film explores themes of double cross, hidden cache,
headstrong son, hell unleashed, old west legend.

19
01:34:03,000 --> 01:34:09,000
The tone is emotional.
